course: dictionary
lesson: 4463
title: How hard is hard?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hardness is how well something resists being scratched, dented or pressed. Scientists use it to tell materials apart. «Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how they break.» So hardness is one of the clues they use.
explain: You can test hardness by scratching. «Hardness of minerals is compared by scratching: a harder mineral scratches a softer one.» Try it with a fingernail, a coin or a nail. If the nail leaves a mark on a material, that material is softer than the nail.
explain: The same word can describe water or people. Hard water has minerals, like calcium, dissolved in it, and it leaves white limescale in kettles. Hardness can also mean being harsh or unkind, as in hardness of heart. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Hardness means how well something resists being scratched, dented or pressed.
fact: «Diamond is the hardest natural mineral.»
fact: The Mohs scale ranks minerals from talc (1, softest) to diamond (10, hardest).
fact: Hard water has minerals like calcium dissolved in it, and it leaves white limescale in kettles.
fact: Hardness can also mean being harsh or unkind, as in hardness of heart.
exercise: «Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how they break.» What is hardness? | *How well something resists being scratched, dented or pressed | How much something weighs | How bright something shines | How something smells
exercise: You scratch a material with your fingernail and it leaves a mark. Which is harder? | They are the same | Neither can be harder | *The fingernail | The material
exercise: Which natural mineral is the hardest? | *Diamond | Talc | Gold | Chalk
test: Hard water leaves white limescale in kettles. What does hard water contain? | Sugar | Salt that you can see | Air bubbles | *Minerals like calcium dissolved in it
test: Hardness of heart means: | Being happy and kind | Being very strong | Having a hard shell | *Being harsh or unkind
exam: On the Mohs scale, from 1 (softest) to 10 (hardest), what number is diamond? | 1 | 5 | *10 | 7
